{#- Guidance Layer -#}
Only extract character state changes. Return an empty array when no explicit changes exist.

## Fact Source Boundary (P0)
- Only extract character state changes from the final text / `chapter_text` corresponding to FinalArtifact.
- Prior state snapshots, authoritative gender, and summary_exit are only for reference, not new state sources.
- Do not write position, identity, emotional state, item, knowledge, or life/death state without textual evidence from the main text.

## Output Field Description
- `character_state_deltas`: Character state change list, each containing character name, change dimension (alive/location/emotional_state/inventory/knowledge/social_status), prior state value, post-state value, and textual evidence.

{% if shared_evidence_anchor %}
## Shared Evidence Anchor
{{ shared_evidence_anchor | tojson(indent=2) }}
Use this as the common basis for this fragment; dimension-specific information can only supplement, not overwrite, anchor facts.
{% endif %}

## Chapter Anchor
- Chapter {{ chapter_number }}
{% if summary_exit %}{{ summary_exit | tojson(indent=2) }}{% endif %}

## Known Characters
{% for name in known_characters %}- {{ name }}{% endfor %}

{% if authoritative_character_genders %}
## Authoritative Character Genders (Highest Priority)
{% for name, gender in authoritative_character_genders.items() %}
- {{ name }}: {{ gender }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% if prior_character_snapshots %}
## Prior Character State (Only Output Changes in This Chapter)
{% for cs in prior_character_snapshots %}
- {{ cs.name }}: location={{ cs.location }}, emotional_state={{ cs.emotional_state }}{% if cs.social_status %}, social_status={{ cs.social_status }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

## Main Text
{{ chapter_text }}

## Requirements
- Maximum {{ max_character_state_deltas | default(8) }} entries.
- Only output when there are actual changes in alive/location/emotional_state/inventory/knowledge/social_status.

## Quality Calibration
- Work Identity: You are an evidence-prioritized narrative fact extractor, skilled at extracting traceable, mergeable state information from main text and upstream anchors.
- Extraction Path: First locate explicit facts in the main text, then cross-reference with shared anchors and known states, and finally only preserve information consumable by downstream mergers.
- Evidence Calibration: Maintain consistency when upstream fragments have confirmed the same fact; use conservative field values to express unknown or pending confirmation when evidence is insufficient.
- Actionable Path: Each piece of information must serve canon, memory, state, or audit chain; avoid treating tone, metaphor, or speculation as fact.

## Pre-Delivery Verification
- Are P0/P1/P2 priorities maintained, and has weak reference not overridden hard constraints?
- Can key judgments be traced back to input evidence, upstream contracts, or approved plans?
- Are unauthorized characters, locations, world rules, future payoffs, or format agreements avoided?
- Are factual boundaries for downstream merging/retrieval preserved, and has speculation not been written as established fact?

